inst/doc
docs/
*.code-workspace
# Claude Code worktrees (agent isolation; do not commit)
.claude/
# Logo art (not part of the package build)
logo_soilkey.png
# Locally rendered vignette HTML (regenerated by R CMD build)
vignettes/*.html
vignettes/*_files/
# R CMD check scratch dirs (regenerated each run)
*.Rcheck/
# Local-only PROJ/GDAL env (.Rbuildignore'd; per-machine paths)
.Renviron
/soil_data/
.positai
# Local working material, not part of the package (kept out of sync)
/Manuscript/
/munsellinterpol-conditions/
/correspondence/
# Credentials. Never commit these.
#
# .gitignore alone is not protection -- it does not stop `git add -f`, and it
# does not follow a file that gets renamed. The real guard is the pre-commit
# hook, which inspects what is actually staged, by filename AND by content
# (see .git/hooks/pre-commit; install it in a fresh clone with
# `cp deploy/hooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/ && chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-commit`).
stripe_backup_code.txt
*backup_code*
*recovery_code*
*recovery-codes*
.env
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json
service_account*.json
